   "text": "L47"
  },
  {
   "id": "hash11",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": -864,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 64,
   "text": "**hash 2-grams, 3-grams**  \n8 hashes each → 16 ids / token",
   "color": "#d946ef"
  },
  {
   "id": "ngid12",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1124,
   "y": -760,
   "width": 51,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl13",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1320,
   "y": -770,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`n-gram ids [T, 16]`"
  },
  {
   "id": "ngt14",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1000,
   "y": -706,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 64,
   "text": "**n-gram table** lookup — 16 rows × 160  \n51.20B · 320 001 536 rows",
   "color": "#d946ef"
  },
  {
   "id": "nge15",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1048,
   "y": -602,
   "width": 205,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl16",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1320,
   "y": -612,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`e_ngram [T, 16×160 = 2560]`"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-gdn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -254,
   "width": 480,
   "height": 230,
   "text": "**Gated DeltaNet rows** (36): linear attention as in Qwen3.5. Each layer keeps one recurrent state [48 heads × 128 × 128] = 786 432 values, the same size at any T — no growing KV cache. New here: the output gate is **sigmoid** (`output_gate_type`), Qwen3.5 used SiLU."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-full",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": 6,
   "width": 480,
   "height": 270,
   "text": "**QSA rows** (12, L3, L7, …): Qwen3.5's gated GQA attention (24 q : 2 KV heads × 256, RoPE on 64 dims) made sparse. A 4-head MQA indexer (1.6M) mean-pools keys over 4-token blocks, scores them and keeps the top 512 blocks = 2048 tokens per query. Cache per token: 1 024 K/V values + a 128-dim indexer key."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-ple",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": 306,
   "width": 480,
   "height": 290,
   "text": "**n-gram PLE** (L1 only, `ple_layer_ids` [2] is one-indexed): the previous 2 token ids are hashed (XOR of multiplied ids, mod 16 distinct primes ≥ 20 000 000) into one table of **51.20B** params — stored as 128 shards, 320 001 536 rows × 160. Per token it is 16 row lookups, so it costs memory, not compute. History resets at EOS."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-moe",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1600,
   "y": -214,
   "width": 460,
   "height": 230,
   "text": "**MoE in every layer**: softmax router over 512 experts → top-10, weights renormalised. Expert = SwiGLU 2560→640→2560 (4.9M). Shared expert (same width) added through a sigmoid gate. Per token: 10 + 1 of 512 experts → ~2.1% of FFN weights."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-gres",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2100,
   "y": -214,
   "width": 460,
   "height": 300,
   "text": "**Gated residual** replaces pre-norm + add. Before each mixer and each MoE: RMSNorm per lane, read gate σ(up(SiLU(down(H)))) with a rank-320 bottleneck, average the 4 gated lanes → one 2560-wide input. The block output is added back to every lane × its own scalar 2σ(·). 6.6M per gate, 96 gates + a final mixer = 640.6M. There is no separate input / post-attention / final RMSNorm."
  },
  {
   "id": "img17",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -630,
   "y": -960,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**image / video** frames",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "patch18",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -541,
   "y": -864,
   "width": 123,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl19",
   "type": "text",
